# Book REST API - Educational Implementation

## Overview

This is a comprehensive educational implementation of a REST API for managing books using Node.js and Express.js. The API follows REST conventions strictly, implements proper error handling with custom error classes, includes validation middleware, and provides detailed JSDoc documentation throughout. We use in-memory storage (an array) to keep the example focused on API concepts without database complexity, while still demonstrating all CRUD operations plus filtering and statistics.

The code is organized into separate modules for data storage, error handling, routes, and middleware - following separation of concerns principles that are essential in production applications. Every function includes comprehensive documentation explaining not just what it does, but why certain patterns were chosen.

